# Internationalization (i18n) Guide

---
description: Complete guide for react-i18next implementation in BB-VoxData Frontend
globs: ["src/features/**/locales/**/*", "src/locales/**/*", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

## Core Principles

Internationalization uses **react-i18next** with modular JSON organization. All UI text must be localized - **no hardcoded strings allowed**. Language switching is dynamic and persisted in Local Storage.

## File Structure & Organization

### Directory Architecture

```
src/
├── locales/
│   ├── i18n.ts                     # Central configuration & setup
│   ├── de/common.json              # Global German translations
│   └── en/common.json              # Global English translations
└── features/
    └── [feature]/
        └── locales/
            ├── de/[namespace].json  # Feature-specific German
            └── en/[namespace].json  # Feature-specific English
```

### File Responsibility Matrix

| File/Directory | Scope | Content Type |
|---|---|---|
| `src/locales/i18n.ts` | Global | Configuration, namespace registration, language detection |
| `src/locales/[lang]/common.json` | Global | Navigation, footer, shared UI elements |
| `src/features/[feature]/locales/[lang]/[namespace].json` | Feature | Feature-specific content, forms, error messages |

## Translation Structure Standards

### JSON Organization Pattern

Every translation file must follow this structure:

```json
{
  "title": "Feature Title",
  "button": {
    "save": "Save",
    "cancel": "Cancel"
  },
  "error": {
    "network": "Network error occurred"
  },
  "a11y": {
    "main": "Main content area",
    "saveButton": "Save your changes",
    "formSection": "User input form"
  }
}
```

### Accessibility (a11y) Requirements

**MANDATORY**: All accessibility attributes must be localized under the `a11y` key:

- **ARIA labels** (`aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`)
- **Screen reader texts** for dynamic content
- **Form field descriptions** and error announcements
- **Navigation landmarks** and section descriptions

#### a11y Key Naming Conventions

| Element Type | Naming Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Buttons | `[action]Button` | `saveButton`, `deleteButton` |
| Forms | `[purpose]Form` | `loginForm`, `contactForm` |
| Sections | `[content]Section` | `navigationSection`, `contentSection` |
| Status | `[state]Status` | `loadingStatus`, `errorStatus` |

## Component Integration Patterns

### useTranslation Hook Usage

**Single Namespace** (most common):
```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation('featureName');
```

**Multiple Namespaces** (when mixing feature + global content):
```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation(['featureName', 'common']);
```

### Accessibility Implementation

Always localize accessibility attributes:
```tsx
<form aria-label={t('a11y.loginForm')}>
  <input aria-label={t('a11y.emailInput')} />
  <button aria-label={t('a11y.submitButton')}>
    {t('button.submit')}
  </button>
</form>
```

## Feature Development Workflow

### 1. Planning Phase
- **Identify all user-facing text** in the feature
- **Map text to appropriate namespace** (feature vs. common)
- **Plan accessibility requirements** and screen reader needs

### 2. Structure Setup
```
features/newFeature/
├── locales/
│   ├── de/newFeature.json
│   └── en/newFeature.json
└── components/
```

### 3. Translation File Creation
- **Start with English** as base language
- **Include a11y section** from the beginning
- **Use consistent key structure** across languages

### 4. Namespace Registration
- **Add imports** to `src/locales/i18n.ts`
- **Register in resources object** for all languages
- **Add to namespace array** in configuration

## Language Management

### Adding New Languages

1. **Create directory structure** for new language code
2. **Copy translation files** from existing language
3. **Translate all content** including a11y keys
4. **Register in i18n.ts** configuration
5. **Update language selector** components

### Translation Key Guidelines

| Key Type | Structure | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Simple text | `keyName` | `title`, `description` |
| Grouped actions | `group.action` | `button.save`, `error.network` |
| Accessibility | `a11y.element` | `a11y.saveButton`, `a11y.mainSection` |

## Quality Assurance

### Pre-Development Checklist
- [ ] No hardcoded strings in any component
- [ ] All ARIA attributes use `t('a11y.key')`
- [ ] Translation keys follow naming conventions
- [ ] Both German and English files created
- [ ] Namespace registered in i18n.ts

### Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- **Hardcoded ARIA labels**: `aria-label="Save"` ❌
- **Mixed localized/hardcoded**: `"Welcome " + t('user.name')` ❌
- **Missing a11y keys**: No accessibility translations ❌
- **Unregistered namespaces**: Using namespace without registration ❌

## Integration with Design System

### Component Localization
- **Form components** must accept localized labels and errors
- **Button variants** should support localized text
- **Modal/Dialog** components need localized titles and actions
- **Status indicators** require localized announcements for screen readers

### Responsive Text Handling
- **Short/long text variants** for responsive layouts
- **Truncation considerations** for different language lengths
- **Icon-only buttons** still need `aria-label` translations

This structure ensures consistent, accessible, and maintainable internationalization across the entire BB-VoxData frontend while supporting future expansion to additional languages and features.